course: dictionary
lesson: 15074
title: The meaning of rightness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rightness is a noun, and it is a word about what is good, fair and correct. It is a quality that a thing, an action or a choice can have. You can see it in people's actions too: «Sam thought about the rightness of telling the teacher the truth.» Here Sam is thinking about whether telling the truth is the good and fair thing to do.
explain: Rightness has two main meanings. The first is about morals: being good, fair or honest. The second is about being correct or suitable. «The judge explained the rightness of the decision» means the judge showed why the decision was fair. «Mum liked the rightness of the blue cushion on the green sofa» means the cushion suited the sofa well.
explain: Look at the words around rightness to find its meaning. Phrases like «rightness and wrongness» or «a sense of rightness» show that it is about what feels good, fair or correct. Ask yourself: is this about what is fair, or about what fits? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Rightness means the quality of being morally right, good or fair.
fact: Rightness also means the quality of being correct or suitable.
fact: «Rightness and wrongness» means whether something is good or bad, and people often discuss it in ethics and religious education.
fact: Rightness is uncountable, so we say «the rightness» or «a sense of rightness», not «a rightness» or «rightnesses».
fact: A good check is to swap in the word «fairness» or «suitability» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Ella felt a sense of rightness when she returned the lost purse.» What does rightness mean here? | Feeling sleepy after a long day | Feeling cold and wet after the rain | *Feeling that doing good was the fair thing | Feeling that she had lost something important
exercise: «The class talked about the rightness of telling a lie to protect a friend.» What are they discussing? | The weather on the day of the trip | Which friend is the tallest in the group | The number of words in a lie | *Whether the action is morally right or wrong
exercise: «The judge explained the rightness of the decision.» Copy the word that names the quality of being fair and correct. | explained | decision | *rightness | judge
test: «Many people debate the rightness and wrongness of breaking a promise.» What does rightness and wrongness mean here? | Whether a door is open or shut | How loud a voice is | *Whether an action is good or bad | How long a promise lasts
test: «Mum liked the rightness of the blue cushion on the green sofa.» Which meaning fits best? | Being morally good | Being very heavy | *Being suitable and matching well | Being very old
exam: Which sentence uses rightness correctly? | She counted two rightnesses in the story. | *She felt a sense of rightness about her choice. | They painted the rightnesses on the wall. | He bought three rightnesses at the shop.
